  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints : $I=\\int_0^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\sin ^4 \\mathrm{x} d \\mathrm{dx} \\quad \\cos \\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{f}, \\sin \\mathrm{d} \\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{dt}$\n$=-\\int_1^0\\left(1-t^2\\right) d t=\\int_0^2\\left(t^4-2 t^2+1\\right) d t$\n$=\\frac{1}{5}\\left(\\mathrm{t}^5\\right)_0^1-\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\mathrm{t}^3\\right)_0^1+(\\mathrm{t})_0^1==\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{2}{5}+1=\\frac{3-10+15}{15}=\\frac{8}{15}$",
    "image": null
  },
